==English==
{{wikipedia|Characterization}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[characterise]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|characterizare}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|χαρακτηρίζω||to designate by a characteristic mark|lang=grc}}, from {{term|χαρακτήρ||a mark, character|lang=grc}}. Synchronically analyzable as {{suffix|character|ize|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈkɛɹəktəɹaɪz/|/ˈkæɹəktəɹaɪz/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈkæɹəktəɹaɪz/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|char|ac|ter|ize|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|characteriz}}

# to depict someone or something a particular way (often negative)
# to determine the characteristics of
